  <div class="pd-content">
    <h2 class="pd-title">VASP Liability Insurance (Virtual Asset Service Providers)</h2>
    <section class="pd-broker-note" aria-label="Insurance broker note">
      <div class="pd-broker-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</div>
      <div class="pd-broker-body">
        <span class="pd-broker-tag">From a licensed insurance broker</span>
        <p class="pd-broker-text">
          <strong>N2N Insurance Brokerage</strong> does not represent any single insurer — it <strong>independently represents the client</strong>
          as an FSS-registered broker (Reg. No. 2026-012201). We compare the wordings, rates and service of AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz
          to propose the <strong>cover and price best suited to your risk</strong>. Each insurer's full wording is provided at application and binding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="pd-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="pd-tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" role="tab">Overview</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" role="tab">Cover</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" role="tab">How to apply</button>
    </div>

    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>VASP liability insurance indemnifies the legal liability of a <strong>virtual-asset service provider</strong> — a crypto exchange, custody business or wallet operator — to its users for losses caused by <strong>hacking, system failure or insider fraud</strong> in the safekeeping and operation of customer assets.</p>
        <p>Operators reported and accepted as a VASP under the <strong>Specific Financial Information Act</strong> are required, together with the <strong>Virtual Asset User Protection Act</strong>, to maintain a user-protection reserve or equivalent insurance; this policy can be used to satisfy that requirement, subject to insurer underwriting.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Compulsory line for reported VASPs</strong>
            <p>Designed for exchanges, custody and wallet operators that are reported VASPs under the Specific Financial Information Act.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Substitute for the statutory reserve</strong>
            <p>Can satisfy the user-protection reserve obligation under the Virtual Asset User Protection Act through insurance, subject to underwriting.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Hacking, system failure, insider fraud</strong>
            <p>Covers the core custody and operational perils — private-key theft, smart-contract exploits, outages and employee/officer misappropriation.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Incident-response costs</strong>
            <p>Restoration, legal, consulting, defense and forensic-investigation costs are addressed alongside user indemnity.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Crypto exchanges</strong>
            <p>Operators running a virtual-asset trading platform for customers.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Custody &amp; wallet operators</strong>
            <p>Custody (Custody) businesses and wallet operators holding customer assets.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Reported VASPs</strong>
            <p>Providers reported and accepted under the Specific Financial Information Act.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Reserve-substitution cases</strong>
            <p>Operators choosing to meet the statutory user-protection reserve through insurance.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>External hacking — private-key theft and smart-contract exploits</li>
          <li>System failure — transaction errors arising from a system outage</li>
          <li>Insider fraud — misappropriation of assets by employees or officers</li>
          <li>Hot-wallet attacks and response to DDoS / APT attacks</li>
          <li>Breach of customer personal data</li>
          <li>Restoration, legal, consulting, defense and forensic-investigation costs</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Statutory basis</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>The Specific Financial Information Act governs VASP reporting and operating duties</li>
          <li>The Virtual Asset User Protection Act requires a user-protection reserve or equivalent insurance</li>
          <li>How the policy satisfies the legal requirement is confirmed with the insurer at underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Willful acts and fraud by the insured</li>
          <li>Market-price movement or FX loss (decline in asset value)</li>
          <li>The operator's own KRW / cash losses</li>
          <li>Incidents occurring during non-compliant (regulatory-breach) operation</li>
          <li>Market manipulation and wash trading</li>
          <li>Nuclear, war and acts of state</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Intended for VASPs reported and accepted under the Specific Financial Information Act</li>
          <li>May satisfy the statutory user-protection reserve through insurance, subject to underwriting</li>
          <li>Incidents during operation that does not meet reporting/certification requirements are excluded</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Corporate documents</strong>
            <p>Business-registration certificate, corporate register and the VASP report-acceptance certificate.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Security &amp; controls</strong>
            <p>ISMS / ISMS-P certification, internal-control overview and the cold/hot-wallet ratio.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Scale &amp; activity</strong>
            <p>Average daily trading volume, custody AUM and a 6-month monthly transaction summary.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Loss history</strong>
            <p>Any past hacking or outage incidents that could give rise to a claim.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Price movement and investment loss are not covered — this policy covers custody and operational incidents</li>
          <li>Confirm precisely how the policy meets the statutory reserve requirement before binding</li>
          <li>Final terms, sub-limits and premium are confirmed after insurer underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>

